SQLineage parsing

This repository contains parsing code adapted from:
https://github.com/cangelosilima/SyncSQL
Source revision: bbfb21916c8c9078ef7c4b947f07bd154b112249

Adapted source includes TSqlParserFactory, the SQL Server legacy grammar fallback,
and the Oracle analyzer's exclusive prediction-cache leasing, limits and simulator setup.
The migration introduces standalone parser facades, structured diagnostics and scoped sessions.
Original source copyright notices, where present, are preserved. See PROVENANCE.md.

The Oracle grammar is supplied by SQLineage.Grammar.PlSql, derived from antlr/grammars-v4's
sql/plsql grammar. Its package retains its Apache-2.0 license, upstream attribution and NOTICE,
including the documented local EDITIONABLE/NONEDITIONABLE synonym syntax changes.
ScriptDom, the ANTLR runtime and other third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.

This repository's Apache-2.0 selection does not change the private SQLineage product's license.
